 hydroxyl group of the serine supplies its oxygen atom to form the C-terminus of the beta chain, while the remainder of the serine residue undergoes an oxidative deamination to produce ammonia and the pyruvoyl prosthetic group on the alpha chain. During this reaction, the Ser that is part of the protease active site of the proenzyme becomes the pyruvoyl prosthetic group, which constitutes an essential element of the active site of the mature decarboxylase"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_00663"}],"value":"Belongs to the phosphatidylserine decarboxylase family. PSD-B subfamily. Prokaryotic type II sub-subfamily"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":259,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Phosphatidylserine decarboxylase beta chain","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_00663"}],"featureId":"PRO_0000029729"},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":260,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":301,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Phosphatidylserine decarboxylase alpha chain","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_00663"}],"featureId":"PRO_0000029730"},{"type":"Active site","location":{"start":{"value":117,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":117,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Charge relay system; for autoendoproteolytic cleavage activity","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_00663"}]},{"type":"Active site","location":{"start":{"value":173,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":173,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Charge relay system; for autoendoproteolytic cleavage activity","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_00663"}]},{"type":"Active site","location":{"start":{"value":260,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":260,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Charge relay 